{
  "area": "skills-effect-terms",
  "description": "How a taken node’s effects leave the module as TEXT (PL.core-unpinned-corpus-cases, U106(6)): the `skill_node_unlocked` event’s `effects: string[]` that `SkillProgression.unlock` raises and the `skill_node_effect/2` facts `skillTreeFacts` publishes, both written by `effectTerm`. Each case carries one authored tree, the node an actor takes from it, the actor’s pool for that tree and the fully resolved SkillTuning; the nodes ask nothing a KB must answer, so a harness reproduces the take with no KB. `expected.event` is the whole event, its `effects` one term per authored effect in authored order — `unlocks(introduce_self)`, never a JSON object; `expected.facts` is every `skill_node_effect(Node, Term).` line for the tree, in authored order. Atoms and the node id are quoted by `prologAtom` (single quotes unless the text is an unquoted-atom token, a backslash and an apostrophe escaped with a backslash), numbers are written as `String` writes them, and an effect with no arguments is its bare kind. Regenerate with `npm run skill-resolution-corpus`.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "an-action-atom-is-written-bare",
      "note": "THE case: `unlocks(introduce_self)` leaves the module as the TEXT `unlocks(introduce_self)`, in the event and in the fact alike — a Prolog term, not a JSON object. A number is written as the number it is, a negative one with its sign and a fraction as the shortest decimal that reads back to it (`String`), and arguments are separated by a comma and one space.",
      "input": {
        "actor": "wren",
        "tree": {
          "id": "first_words",
          "skill": "speaking",
          "nodes": [
            {
              "parents": [],
              "requires": [],
              "effects": [
                {
                  "kind": "unlocks",
                  "args": [
                    "introduce_self"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "kind": "modifies",
                  "args": [
                    "reach",
                    2
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "kind": "modifies",
                  "args": [
                    "energy_cost",
                    -1
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "kind": "modifies",
                  "args": [
                    "stride",
                    0.5
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "id": "greetings",
              "tree": "first_words",
              "cost": 1
            }
          ]
        },
        "node": "greetings",
        "points": 1,
        "tuning": {
          "pointsPerLevel": 1,
          "defaultNodeCost": 1,
          "defaultMaxLevel": 10,
          "levelXp": [
            0,
            0,
            100,
            250,
            450,
            700,
            1000,
            1350,
            1750,
            2200,
            2700
          ],
          "advanceAction": "train_skill",
          "unlockAction": "unlock_skill_node"
        }
      },
      "expected": {
        "event": {
          "type": "skill_node_unlocked",
          "actorId": "wren",
          "nodeId": "greetings",
          "treeId": "first_words",
          "cost": 1,
          "effects": [
            "unlocks(introduce_self)",
            "modifies(reach, 2)",
            "modifies(energy_cost, -1)",
            "modifies(stride, 0.5)"
          ]
        },
        "facts": [
          "skill_node_effect(greetings, unlocks(introduce_self)).",
          "skill_node_effect(greetings, modifies(reach, 2)).",
          "skill_node_effect(greetings, modifies(energy_cost, -1)).",
          "skill_node_effect(greetings, modifies(stride, 0.5))."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "an-argument-that-is-not-an-atom-token-is-quoted",
      "note": "An argument that is not an unquoted-atom token (`^[a-z][a-zA-Z0-9_]*$`) is single-quoted by `prologAtom`, and an apostrophe inside it is escaped as `\\'`: a space (`Old Mill`), a capital first letter (`Riposte`, which unquoted is a Prolog VARIABLE and would unify with anything), an apostrophe (`smith’s_mark` spelled with a plain one) and a leading digit (`2nd_wind`). A port that writes them bare publishes a fact the KB reads as something else, or cannot read at all.",
      "input": {
        "actor": "wren",
        "tree": {
          "id": "first_words",
          "skill": "speaking",
          "nodes": [
            {
              "parents": [],
              "requires": [],
              "effects": [
                {
                  "kind": "permits",
                  "args": [
                    "Old Mill"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "kind": "unlocks",
                  "args": [
                    "Riposte"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "kind": "permits",
                  "args": [
                    "smith's_mark"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "kind": "unlocks",
                  "args": [
                    "2nd_wind"
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "id": "market_talk",
              "tree": "first_words",
              "cost": 1
            }
          ]
        },
        "node": "market_talk",
        "points": 1,
        "tuning": {
          "pointsPerLevel": 1,
          "defaultNodeCost": 1,
          "defaultMaxLevel": 10,
          "levelXp": [
            0,
            0,
            100,
            250,
            450,
            700,
            1000,
            1350,
            1750,
            2200,
            2700
          ],
          "advanceAction": "train_skill",
          "unlockAction": "unlock_skill_node"
        }
      },
      "expected": {
        "event": {
          "type": "skill_node_unlocked",
          "actorId": "wren",
          "nodeId": "market_talk",
          "treeId": "first_words",
          "cost": 1,
          "effects": [
            "permits('Old Mill')",
            "unlocks('Riposte')",
            "permits('smith\\'s_mark')",
            "unlocks('2nd_wind')"
          ]
        },
        "facts": [
          "skill_node_effect(market_talk, permits('Old Mill')).",
          "skill_node_effect(market_talk, unlocks('Riposte')).",
          "skill_node_effect(market_talk, permits('smith\\'s_mark')).",
          "skill_node_effect(market_talk, unlocks('2nd_wind'))."
        ]
      }
    },
